# --- Site visibility ---
# launch (the production default): ONLY the homepage responds — methodology,
# rankings, lab, admin, run replays, stock dossiers, and the run APIs all 404,
# the homepage renders zero outbound links, and its board preview is a static
# MOCKUP LEADERBOARD (redacted tickers; no DB reads, no real data).
# full (the development default): everything visible. Email capture works in
# both modes. Set explicitly to override either default.
# MAG8_SITE_MODE=launch

# --- Auth for real pipeline runs (one of the two) ---
# Option A: Claude API key — per-token billing to your API account.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Option B: Claude subscription (Pro/Max) — no API billing; runs draw on your
# plan's usage limits. Nothing to set if this machine has a logged-in Claude
# Code CLI (detected automatically). On a server, mint a long-lived token with
# `claude setup-token` and set it here:
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# Detection override: `subscription` asserts subscription auth when it can't be
# seen on disk (e.g. macOS Keychain); `disabled` blocks real runs entirely.
# MAG8_AUTH_MODE=subscription

# --- Required to trigger runs from /admin in production ---
# Any long random string. In development, admin access is open when this is unset.
ADMIN_TOKEN=

# --- Optional overrides (defaults shown) ---
# MAG8_DISCOVERY_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# MAG8_LENS_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# MAG8_COMPILER_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# MAG8_MAX_CONCURRENT_STOCKS=3
# MAG8_DB_PATH=./db/mag8.db
# MAG8_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT_MS=720000
# MAG8_LENS_TIMEOUT_MS=900000
# MAG8_COMPILE_TIMEOUT_MS=360000
# MAG8_RUN_TIMEOUT_MS=5400000
# MAG8_MOCK_SPEED=1
# Allow zero-spend mock runs on a production/staging deployment (dev always allows them).
# MAG8_ALLOW_MOCK=1

# --- Reasoning-cost knobs (the real constraint on subscription auth is the
# --- plan's 5-hour usage window; lower effort = longer window survivability).
# Effort per stage: low | medium | high | xhigh | max (SDK default high).
# Lens defaults medium per the 2026-07-06 A/B: at high a lens cell blew the
# then-$1 per-call cap and died; at medium it completed (~$0.69, 18 links).
# That cap is gone (2026-09-04), so high no longer ends a cell early — it does
# still draw harder on the 5-hour window, which is why medium stays default.
# MAG8_DISCOVERY_EFFORT=high
# MAG8_LENS_EFFORT=medium
# MAG8_COMPILER_EFFORT=medium
# Thinking override per stage: adaptive | disabled (unset = SDK default).
# MAG8_DISCOVERY_THINKING=
# MAG8_LENS_THINKING=
# MAG8_COMPILER_THINKING=
# Optional per-call USD caps. UNSET = UNCAPPED, and that is the default: the
# SDK ends the call at the cap with error_max_budget_usd, so the research
# already paid for is discarded and the cell persists as an error. The timeout,
# MAG8_MAX_TURNS_* and the run watchdog bound a call without losing its work.
# Set a positive number to arm one anyway (0 or blank leaves it disarmed):
# MAG8_DISCOVERY_MAX_USD=
# MAG8_LENS_MAX_USD=
# MAG8_COMPILE_MAX_USD=

# --- SEC EDGAR (free, keyless — used by the universe screen and the Bottleneck desk) ---
# SEC requires a descriptive User-Agent identifying the app and a contact address;
# requests without one are rejected with 403. Format: "AppName contact@example.com".
# MAG8_EDGAR_UA takes precedence; MAG8_SEC_UA is the older name and still works.
# MAG8_EDGAR_UA=Mag8 you@example.com

# --- Grounding checks ---
# Independent quote cross-check (Yahoo, free, fail-silent) runs on every real
# run between analysis and compile; >15% divergence vs a lens's spot price
# becomes a disclosed gap note. Set to 0 to disable (e.g. air-gapped deploys).
# MAG8_PRICE_CHECK=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Tide (market conditions desk). Every dial is editable from /admin; these
# only set the baseline the panel diffs against. MAG8_TIDE=0 switches the whole
# desk off, and it is checked per call — supreme over every other setting.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MAG8_TIDE=1
# MAG8_TIDE_HISTORY_YEARS=30
# MAG8_TIDE_PCT_WINDOW_YEARS=20
# MAG8_TIDE_BREADTH=1            # counting breadth is ~500 price requests
# MAG8_TIDE_BREADTH_SIZE=500
# The exposure band. The near-term reading is meant to dominate: valuation says
# little about the coming year, so a large slow penalty would park the desk in
# cash for a decade at a time.
# MAG8_TIDE_EXP_BASE=60
# MAG8_TIDE_EXP_FAST_PENALTY=35
# MAG8_TIDE_EXP_SLOW_PENALTY=10
